  // window, and signature algorithm. A certificate that fails to parse is
  // skipped rather than blinding the whole bundle.
  certificates() []network.certificate
}

// Rule set on an Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI) load balancer
//
// A named collection of rules that listeners attach through ruleSetNames.
// Rules act on requests and responses as they pass through the load balancer.
private oci.loadBalancer.ruleSet @defaults("name") {
  // Rule set name
  name string
  // Rules composing the set
  //
  // Each entry carries an `action` naming the rule kind, for example
  // ADD_HTTP_REQUEST_HEADER, REMOVE_HTTP_RESPONSE_HEADER,
  // CONTROL_ACCESS_USING_HTTP_METHODS, REDIRECT, ALLOW, or
  // HTTP_HEADER. The remaining keys vary by action: header rules carry
  // `header` and `value`, method control carries `allowedMethods` and
  // `statusCode`, redirects carry `conditions` and `redirectUri`, and ALLOW
